**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests`

**How to implement.** The import dialog's pure MVU (001 §B 'The decisions show as one dialog with a row per entry, and nothing is overwritten silently'; 001 §O 'Import dialog: one row per entry, its status, the default action and an override'; .spec-md §3.7, §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 the Apply / Cancel pair; the S3.2 brief). It reaches the import seam only on Apply. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `brush`, `messageColor`, `positiveBackground`, `negativeBackground`, `verbButton` and `actionButton` (the view section, `MaterialsWindowView.fs:877-924`) lose `private`. Their docs say, in no more words, that the import dialog uses the same look: one declaration serves both, the spec 0048 R2 rule `LibraryWindowView.fs` follows for `LifecycleAction`. No body changes, and no other view's copy is touched. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView`, compiled directly after `MaterialsWindowView.fs` and before `MaterialsWindow.fs` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment. The module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §B and spec 0050 S3.2, and every type, case and field has a one-line doc. (a) `ImportDialogRequest` = `SettlePendingCatalogue of PendingCatalogueImport` (a catalogue whose rows wait, step 98) | `ApplyDroppedEntries of decisions : ImportDecision list` (dropped entry files, step 104): what the dialog decides. S4.2 adds a kit snapshot's case. `member this.decisions : ImportDecision list` is the pending import's `decisions` or the dropped ones. `member this.heading : ControlCaption` is `Import from <folder>: <k> entries need a decision.` (`entry.folder` of the pending import) or `Import <n> dropped entry files.`. (b) `ImportDialogApplied = { request : ImportDialogRequest; choices : ImportChoice list; outcome : ImportOutcome }` is what an Apply did. `member this.summary : ControlCaption` is `Imported <folder> (decisions applied: <n>).` or `Imported the dropped entry files (decisions applied: <n>).`, `n` counting the choices. Every opener shows it as its status, so the text is written once. (c) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportDialogContext = { imports : CatalogueImportContext; request : ImportDialogRequest; onApplied : ImportDialogApplied -> unit; requestClose : unit -> unit }`, in the shape of `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`): the composition root bakes the seam, the opener's callback and the window's close, and tests substitute recording stubs. (d) `ImportDiffState` = `NoImportDiffShown` | `ImportDiffShown of LibraryEntryId`: at most one row shows its diff. (e) `ImportDialogModel = { context : ImportDialogContext; choices : ImportChoice list; diff : ImportDiffState; lastError : CatalogueImportError option }`. `initImportDialog (context : ImportDialogContext) : ImportDialogModel` opens with the `byDefault` (step 93) of every decision of `context.request.decisions`, in order, no diff shown and no error. Rows are told apart by their decision's `entryId`, the key `settle` matches choices by (step 99). (f) `ImportDialogMsg`, each case documented: `DecideImportRow of LibraryEntryId` (the row takes its default action), `OverrideImportRow of LibraryEntryId * ImportAction` (the row takes one of its `alternatives`), `ToggleImportDiff of LibraryEntryId`, `ApplyImportChoices` and `CancelImportDialog`. (g) `updateImportDialog (msg : ImportDialogMsg) (m : ImportDialogModel) : ImportDialogModel`. `DecideImportRow id` sets the row's action to its `defaultAction`. `OverrideImportRow (id, action)` sets it when `action` is one of the row's `alternatives` and is inert otherwise, including for a row the dialog does not hold. Both clear `lastError`. `ToggleImportDiff id` shows that row's diff, or hides it when it is the one shown. `ApplyImportChoices` is the only message that reaches the seam: for `SettlePendingCatalogue p` it calls `context.imports.settle p m.choices` (step 99), and for `ApplyDroppedEntries _` it calls `context.imports.apply m.choices` (step 94). `Ok outcome` calls `context.onApplied { request = context.request; choices = m.choices; outcome = outcome }`, then `context.requestClose ()`, and clears `lastError`. `Error e` sets `lastError` to `Some e`, and the dialog stays open with its choices. `CancelImportDialog` calls `context.requestClose ()` and nothing else. (h) `importDialogView (m : ImportDialogModel) (dispatch : ImportDialogMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel`. Docked at the bottom is one horizontal row of `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importApplyButton (ControlCaption "Apply") positiveBackground` and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importCancelButton (ControlCaption "Cancel") negativeBackground`: one row, the boxes' margin as the gap, distinct colours, the look of the Select / Close pair. Above it, when `lastError` is `Some e`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importDialogMessage` shows `e.caption` (step 101) in `messageColor`. Docked at the top, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importDialogHeading` shows `request.heading` and the line `Nothing is imported until you press Apply.`. A `ScrollViewer` fills the rest; its vertical `StackPanel` carries `importDecisionList` and holds one block per choice. A row's block carries `importDecisionRow entryId.uiKey` and holds, in order: a line with the decision's `rowName`, its `kind.caption`, `version <v>` (the incoming content's version, or the held latest for `EntryUnlisted`) and `status.caption`; the line `Default: <decision.actionCaption decision.defaultAction>`; a `WrapPanel` holding one box per offered action, the default first and then the `alternatives` in order, each carrying `importActionOption entryId.uiKey action.uiKey` with `decision.actionCaption action` as its label. The chosen one is an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others are `verbButton`s. Pressing the default dispatches `DecideImportRow`, and an alternative `OverrideImportRow`. The `WrapPanel` sits in the vertical block, so it wraps at the window's width (AGENTS.md: never in a horizontal `StackPanel`). When the row has a diff base, a `verbButton` carrying `importDiffToggle entryId.uiKey`, labelled `Show diff` or `Hide diff` while shown, dispatches `ToggleImportDiff`. While shown, a block carrying `importDiffPreview entryId.uiKey` lists the lines of `incoming.diffFrom held` (step 106), one `TextBlock` each, prefixed `  `, `- ` or `+ `, with removed lines in `messageColor` and added lines in `Color.FromRgb(0uy, 110uy, 0uy)`. The held envelope is read through `context.imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` (step 105) as the view renders, as the library windows' views re-query their stores. An error shows one line with its `describe`, and `None` the line `The held version is not in the library.`. The diff base is: for `DivergentContent (incoming, held)`, the held version equal to the incoming version when `held.versions` holds it, else `held.latest`; for `VersionNotHeld (incoming, held)`, `held.latest`; for `NameCollision (incoming, sameName)`, the entry the row's `RebindToHeldEntry` names when that is its action, else the first of `sameName`, at its latest. `EntryIdNotHeld`, `SameContentHash` and `EntryUnlisted` rows have none. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type LibraryEntryId with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`, its GUID's text, as `CategoryId.uiKey`; `type LibraryEntryKind with member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `Material`, `Sample`, `Source`, `Polarizer`, `Detector`, `Category`; `type ImportStatus with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, in step 93's order: `New entry`, `Already in the library`, `New version of a held entry`, `Differs from the held version`, `Same name as a held entry`, `No longer in its catalogue`; `type ImportAction with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`: `add`, `reuse`, `version-latest`, `version-kept`, `fork`, `rebind-<guid>`, `skip`, `retire`; `type ImportDecision with member this.actionCaption (action : ImportAction) : ControlCaption`: `Add` (`Side by side` on a `NameCollision`), `Reuse the held entry`, `Add version, made latest`, `Add version, latest kept`, `Fork as a new entry`, `Use my <name> instead` (001 §B; the name of the same-name entry it names, or `Use the held entry instead` on any other status), `Skip` and `Mark inactive`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a group after the Materials window's, under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.2: `importDialogWindow` (`"ImportDialogWindow"`), `importDialogHeading` (`"ImportDialogHeading"`), `importDecisionList` (`"ImportDecisionList"`), `importDecisionRow (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportDecisionRow_{entry.value}"`), `importActionOption (entry : ConstructorUiKey) (action : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportActionOption_{entry.value}_{action.value}"`), `importDiffToggle (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportDiffToggle_{entry.value}"`), `importDiffPreview (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$"ImportDiffPreview_{entry.value}"`), `importDialogMessage` (`"ImportDialogMessage"`), `importApplyButton` (`"ImportApplyButton"`) and `importCancelButton` (`"ImportCancelButton"`). (5) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs` (`module ImportDialogTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`), appended to the compile list after `LibraryWindowTests.fs` with no comment. Its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and its dialog context records `onApplied` and `requestClose`. Its rows come from `decideDroppedFiles` (step 104) over files written as step 104's facts write them, in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "ImportDialogTests")`: a new user material, a user material named `Silicon` (a `NameCollision`) and Silicon's built-in version 2 with a changed description (a `VersionNotHeld`). `the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the ten ids' texts. `the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied`: three rows in drop order, each choice its `byDefault`, no diff shown, and `tryHeldEntry` of the new material answers `None`. `an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert`: `OverrideImportRow` of the collision with its `RebindToHeldEntry` takes it; of the new material with `ForkIncomingEntry`, which it does not offer, it is inert; and `DecideImportRow` restores the collision's default. `Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes`: with the collision overridden by `SkipIncomingEntry`, `ApplyImportChoices` leaves the new material held, Silicon held at versions 1 and 2 with latest 1, and no second `Silicon`; it records one `onApplied` whose `choices` are the model's and whose `summary` is `Imported the dropped entry files (decisions applied: 3).`, and one close. `Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue`: a test-local `PendingCatalogueImport`, whose entry names a test-local catalogue id and folder and whose one decision is the collision `decideEntry` gives under `CatalogueImportOrigin (that id, CatalogueName "Lab")`, applied through `ApplyImportChoices`, holds both `Silicon` materials, and `proxy.loggedImports ()` holds a row for that catalogue id. `a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open`: the rows of a dropped new material and a dropped sample that names it, with the material overridden by `SkipIncomingEntry`, answer `lastError = Some (DanglingReferenceErr _)` on Apply, with no `onApplied`, no close and nothing held. `Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing`: `CancelImportDialog` records one close, no `onApplied`, and nothing is held. `each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers`: `importDialogView` mounted headless, as `LibraryWindowTests` mounts a view, shows in the collision's row `Silicon — from <its file>`, `Material`, `version 1`, `Same name as a held entry` and `Default: Side by side`, and the options `Side by side`, `Use my Silicon instead` and `Skip` by their `importActionOption` ids; the new material's row has no `importDiffToggle`. `a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload`: pressing the version row's `importDiffToggle` shows `importDiffPreview` holding a `- ` line with the held description and a `+ ` line with the incoming one; pressing it again hides it.

**Acceptance.** After the dialog's MVU lands, `ImportDialogView` MUST reach the import seam only on `ApplyImportChoices`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied`, `an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert`, `Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes`, `Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue`, `a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open`, `Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing`, `each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers`, `a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload`, the count rising by 9; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.
